  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>Tokenized stocks distributed value rose 9.9% over 30D:</strong> Tokenized equity distributed value at $3.58B (9.9% higher over 30D) shows the early lane still adding balance sheet on a small set of platforms. Related: <a href=\"https://decrypt.co/382145/walmart-blocks-stock-okx-ice-tokenized-trading-venue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Walmart Blocks Its Stock From OKX-ICE Tokenized Trading Venue</a> (Decrypt).</li><li><strong>Near-term progress depends on market plumbing:</strong> broader growth is likely to hinge on broker distribution, custody confidence, and venue interoperability rather than listing count alone.</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Securities and broker-rule constraints often set the pace more than listing count, so near-term share stays tied to venues that can actually distribute products. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/10/31/uber-tests-how-tokenization-can-put-idle-cash-to-work-with-hsbc-franklin-templeton\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Uber tests how tokenization can put idle cash to work with HSBC, Franklin Templeton</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Tokenized stocks remain an early-stage lane:</strong> liquidity and scale are still concentrated in a small set of platforms/networks.</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
